{"id":"uneven-treatment","title":"Like permits, unlike waits","question":"Does the same kind of permit take longer in some parts of the city, or for some kinds of applicant?","finding":"For full-review alterations to one- and two-family houses costing $50,000 to $1 million, issued 2019 to 2026, the citywide median wait was 408 days; it was 530 in Oceanview/Merced/Ingleside and 273 in Presidio Heights. Among counter permits with plans worth $25,000 or more, 26% were issued within a day when the applicant was a licensed contractor and 6% when a permit consultant.","how":"Days from filing to issue for one narrow class of permit, grouped by the neighborhood and supervisor district the City assigns to the address (40 or more permits each), with the share that used a permit consultant and the share whose project drew a public review request. Applicant type is the role of the contact marked as applicant.","limits":"Neighborhoods differ in the buildings they hold: older houses, hillside lots, historic districts and narrow streets draw more reviews under the same rules, and neighbours in some areas ask for review more often. Those differences are in the table so they can be weighed. A slow median is a reason to look at which stations account for it, not a finding of bias.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"place","t":"Place or applicant","type":"text"},{"k":"permits","t":"Permits","type":"int"},{"k":"median","t":"Median days to issue","type":"int"},{"k":"vsCity","t":"Times the citywide median","type":"times"},{"k":"overYear","t":"Share over one year","type":"pct"},{"k":"sameDay","t":"Share issued within a day","type":"pct"},{"k":"consultant","t":"Share with a permit consultant","type":"pct"},{"k":"review","t":"Share with a public review request","type":"pct"},{"k":"stations","t":"Median review stations","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"place":"Supervisor district 1","permits":378,"median":390.0,"vsCity":0.96,"overYear":0.513,"consultant":0.037,"review":0.048,"stations":7.0},{"place"